<title>UK: BNP sets 1.25 bln French franc perpetual bond.</title>
<headline>BNP sets 1.25 bln French franc perpetual bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Banque Nationale de Paris and Merrill Lynch.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BANQUE NATIONALE DE PARIS</p>
<p> AMT    1.25 BLN FFR  COUPON    *6.5	 MATURITY  **PERPETUAL</p>
<p> TYPE   STEP-UP PERP  ISS PRICE  99.907    PAY DATE    21.MAY.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  0.625     REOFFER    99.907    SPREAD	+73 BP</p>
<p> NOTES     *TO YEAR 10 THEN STEPS UP TO 3M PIBOR PLUS 2.0 PCT</p>
<p>	    **CALL AT PAR 21.MAY.07</p>
<p> LISTING    PAR/LUX   DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M CRS DEFLT   NO</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.50	SELL CONC  0.125     PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 10-YEAR OAT CURVE</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>CALL SUBJECT TO PRIOR APPROVAL BY COMMISSION</p>
<p>		BANCAIRE</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
